---

## Issues

- [ ] `description` is 184 chars (under cap, fine).

- [ ] `intent` is 144 words (over cap 100). Drop injectBadge merge history.
  Traces to: `intent` field | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content (migration history)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `outcomes.desired` has 5 items (cap 4). Items 0 and 1 collapse. Item 4
  ("status reports skip when present") is install-service parent invariant.
  Traces to: `outcomes.desired` | Brevity Contract caps + Sibling-redundancy
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Sibling-redundancy

- [ ] `outcomes.undesired` has 5 paragraph-length items with exact before/after
  Markdown shown inline. Trim to 3-4 ≤2 sentences.
  Traces to: `outcomes.undesired` | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `## Strategy` has ~7 decisions (over cap ~5). One ("category absorbs
  injectBadge and retires it") is migration history; another ("README
  creation derives project name from package.json first") encodes specific
  data sources.
  Traces to: `## Strategy` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content (migration history)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `## Good examples` and `## Bad examples` reproduce full Markdown READMEs
  verbatim including the badge URL with exact `img.shields.io/badge/AIDE`
  path, exact heading levels, exact placeholder description text. Cap is
  2-3 brief examples; forbidden content (exact strings, URLs).
  Traces to: examples sections | Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Forbidden-content

- [ ] `## References` has 4 paragraph-length entries. Trim to "path + one-line".
  Traces to: `## References` | Brevity Contract format
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] Carry-forward (prior cycle): 3 unchecked items. Re-walk after rewrite.

## Retro

This spec is moderately bloated by Markdown-template reproduction in
examples. The badge URL is a code-level constant; the examples should
illustrate the placement pattern (badge above heading, after frontmatter,
appended to existing badge strip) without showing the bytes.
